  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the hateful textual message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'when the un adds another million to the holocaust death toll' because the meme's overall intent is to provoke a reaction by making the viewer associate the UN with the Holocaust death toll. The text is the primary vehicle for the hateful message, and the user is implicitly invited to internalize or react to this false equivalence. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the text as a direct statement about the UN's actions creates a projection of responsibility onto the viewer's understanding of the UN's role.",
